.claude/worktrees/
# Session-scoped Claude hook overrides are local-only; tracked project wiring stays authoritative.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Transient test output
test-results/
# ADR-0516 fabric drive-loop OPERATIONAL (execution) plane — repo-adjacent
# claim/heartbeat/run state per specs/fabric-drive-loop-state.json. Never
# committed: the durable coordination plane (plan/fabric-loop/) is the only
# PR-governed loop-state surface; this root is a local bridge store behind
# ExecutionPlanePort until the oya-cloud-ci-loop-state-service cutover.
/.oya-loop-state/
# Generated outputs default to untracked. Public/productized generated
# artifacts that must be committed are force-added intentionally and declared in
# registry/generated-artifact-control-plane.json, where cloud-ci enforces owner,
# generator, materialization, and merge policy. Keep this preventive layer aligned
# with the manifest's generated_path_rules; the Rust gate is authoritative.
**/generated/**
**/__generated__/**
**/generated-sources/**
**/generated-types/**
**/gen/**
**/*.generated.json
**/*.generated.ts
**/*.generated.d.ts
**/*.pb.go
**/*.pb.rs
!**/generated/
!**/generated/.gitkeep
# FROZEN-REFERENCE RATCHET BASELINE — DE-COMMITTED (ADR-0616, supersedes ADR-0596/#828 hotfix).
# The gate-baseline face is the firewall ratchet's frozen reference. It was kept TRACKED only
# because the emitter read it as a committed git blob via `git show <merge-base>:<this-path>`, so
# de-committing it emptied the frozen baseline (missing_at_merge_base=true -> every pre-existing
# debt item read as NEW growth: the #828 deadlock). ADR-0616 removes that committed-blob read: the
# emitter now REGENERATES the frozen reference by running the accounting producer over the merge-base
# SOURCE worktree (ratchet-policy.json declares frozen_reference.source: regenerate-from-merge-base-
# source), validated by a determinism canary + merge-base-tree provenance. With no committed blob to
# empty, de-commit is safe and the deadlock is impossible. It is declared materialization_mode:
# not-tracked-in-git in registry/generated-artifact-control-plane.json and is covered by the broad
# **/*.generated.json rule above — deliberately NOT negated (move-manifest and the other
# de-commit-class faces share that same non-negation posture; none of them re-enter git via `!`).
# ADR-0595/ADR-0597 de-commit class: the SIX cloud-ci faces below are pure derivations
# (git ls-files x OWNERS x ADR front-matter x specs). They were the #1 merge-conflict /
# merge-queue friction because every PR re-materialized multi-MB blobs. They are now DERIVED ON
# DEMAND (buck2 run //ci/facade/generated-artifact-freshness:oya-cloud-ci-materialize-generated-faces-bin) and materialized out-of-graph for
# consumers, whose gates re-derive content from the candidate tree; the freshness gate validates
# regenerate-success + regenerate-twice determinism instead of byte parity, and the control-plane
# gate forbids re-tracking them (materialization_mode: not-tracked-in-git). They are already
# covered by the **/*.generated.json rule above and are intentionally NOT negated here (same as
# move-manifest and gate-baseline — all de-commit-class faces share this posture):
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/accounting-registry.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/decision-crosswalk.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/enforcement-inventory.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/enforcement-liveness.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/ttl-policy.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/scm-facts.generated.json
#   ci/facade/artifact-inventory-registry/adr-census-epoch-receipt.generated.json
# ADR-0597 (completes the ADR-0595 strangler): scm-facts.generated.json was the LAST committed
# pure-derivation face. It was kept committed in #828 only because it is a declared hermetic input
# to ~20 gate tests; those consumers now materialize it on demand (CI producer-regen uploads the
# materialized face; every gate matrix leg downloads it before `cargo test`). De-committing it
# removes the last shared committed merge surface, so a PR can no longer dirty every other open PR
# by re-materializing it — the faces-serialization cascade is now impossible. It is NOT a frozen
# ratchet reference (it is the SCM-facts snapshot the producer derives FROM, regenerated from
# `git ls-files` each run).
# NOTE: gate-baseline.generated.json IS now in the de-commit class too (ADR-0616): the frozen
# reference is regenerated from the merge-base source, so its committed-blob guard was inverted and
# it is de-committed alongside these faces (covered by **/*.generated.json above, not negated).
# ADR-0613 (continues the ADR-0595/0604 de-commit strangler): the two remaining controller-
# materialized PROJECTION faces below were still committed merge surfaces. They are exactly the
# projections a mis-invoked local materializer can silently corrupt (the motivating incident:
# masterplan adr_count 106->64 from a partial regen). They are now DERIVED ON DEMAND by the same
# materializer entrypoint (buck2 run //ci/facade/generated-artifact-freshness:oya-cloud-ci-materialize-generated-faces-bin;
# masterplan first, then the arch-graph dashboard). Freshness is regenerate-success (masterplan-drift
# gate, controller-materialized output_mode) + regenerate-twice determinism (product-graph), not byte
# parity; the control-plane policy gate forbids re-tracking them (materialization_mode: not-tracked-in-git).
#   docs/machine-readable/masterplan.generated.json  (covered by **/*.generated.json above; not negated)
# product-graph.html is a .html (not *.generated.json), so it needs an explicit ignore line:
docs/architecture/product-graph.html
# ADR-0621: active-artifact-contract graph edges are controller-materialized from
# committed contract sources and must never be hand-merged as a readable authority face.
registry/graph/active-artifact-contract-edges.json
# ADR-0614 (amends ADR-0563; finishes the pure-derivation strangler for the LAST committed
# reorg face): move-manifest.generated.json is NO LONGER excluded from the de-commit class — it
# JOINS it. ADR-0563 originally made it the authoritative COMMITTED move-bijection; ADR-0614
# amends that committed-vs-materialized stance. The face is a pure function of the committed
# move-plan(s) x candidate tree, so — like the ADR-0595 faces — it is DERIVED ON DEMAND (buck2 run
# //ci/facade/generated-artifact-freshness:oya-cloud-ci-materialize-generated-faces-bin runs the
# codemod `manifest` subcommand as step 1, materialize_move_manifest, before the scm-facts emitter's
# rename-aware relabel reads it). registry-drift validates regenerate-twice determinism, not
# committed-byte parity; the control-plane policy gate forbids re-tracking it (materialization_mode:
# not-tracked-in-git). It is covered by the broad **/*.generated.json rule above and is intentionally
# NOT negated. The path-resolver `load` is FAIL-CLOSED on absence (ADR-0614 shipped): a missing/
# unreadable file is a hard materialization-precondition error, not a silent identity relabel. A
# present-but-foreign/malformed body still collapses to identity (anti-laundering). The materializer
# writes the manifest as step 1 before any relabel-read leg (audited: no CI leg runs the emitter
# without a preceding materialize step).
# buck2 build output
/buck-out/
# Repo-root build/test SCRATCH artifacts (prevention layer; the cloud-ci-root-workspace-hygiene
# allowlist gate (ADR-0600) + the cloud-ci-total-accounting `scratch_artifact` frozen_empty code
# are the blocking backstops per enforcement-layering: automation default + blocking backstop).
# These root-anchored patterns block the slice-NN burndown / retest / lane-scratch class (#671
# G011 residue + the Jun-10 slice-6 logs + the *-targets.txt / premise / review-verdict pollution)
# from being staged again. Root-anchored so legitimately nested tracked files are untouched;
# force-add (`git add -f`) still routes the file through the allowlist gate, which is the
# construction layer that makes committed root scratch unmergeable (.gitignore alone cannot catch
# `git add -f` or already-tracked files — the gate is the real enforcement).
/*.log
/*.tmp
/*.out
/run-*.sh
/run-slice.sh
/retest-targets.txt
/*-targets.txt
/branch-wired-members.txt
/premise.txt
/review-verdict.txt
/slice*-*.log
/slice*-*.txt
# cloud-kernel QEMU/serial CONFORMANCE run output (build output, not evidence). The
# crate-local cloud/cloud-kernel/.gitignore ignores top-level /out/*.log but NOT the
# out/conformance/ subdir or the .txt report variants, which is how 50 conformance logs +
# stress-summary.txt slipped in via the bulk kernel import (#640). The tracked /out/*.elf
# carriers (include_bytes! build inputs) + musl-src/hello.c stay un-ignored in the crate
# .gitignore; this only adds the run-output subtree.
cloud/cloud-kernel/out/conformance/
cloud/cloud-kernel/out/stress-summary.txt
# Merge-base frozen-baseline snapshot (ADR-0551, FRIC-1781112000): a per-checkout derived
# reference materialized by the scm-facts emitter from `git merge-base <base_ref> HEAD`.
# It varies with the base branch position, so it can never be a committed face; CI
# rematerializes it before gates consume it.
ci/facade/baseline-ratchet/gate-baseline.merge-base.generated.json
# History-volatile SCM facts snapshot (ADR-0552, FRIC-1781234047): per-path last-touch
# revision ids + timestamps, rewritten by every squash-merge — a per-checkout derived input
# materialized by the scm-facts emitter, so it can never be a committed face; CI
ci/facade/scm-facts-snapshot/scm-volatile-facts.generated.json
ci/facade/scm-facts-snapshot/history-only-retirement-facts.generated.json
# Dev-only Asterinas boot-harness receipts are regenerable run outputs (reference target/ logs); not committed.
kernel/asterinas/harness/*/receipts/
# Agent orchestration scratch. Workflow driver scripts (_workflow.js / _wf.js and
# friends) are the MACHINERY that produces an audit, not the audit itself: they carry
# machine-absolute paths, name no owner, and nothing in the build graph references them.
# Harvest the findings, reap the driver. A driver deliberately retained as cited
# provenance (a findings doc quoting one of its constants) must be force-added and say so.
_workflow.js
_wf.js
_prewave*.js
_ralplan_workflow.js
# Machine-local buck2 config. MUST NEVER be committed.
#
# This is the ONLY mechanism that can wire the remote cache: buck2 resolves
# [buck2_re_client] into DaemonStartupConfig from PROJECT CONFIG FILES ONLY, so
# `--config` and `--config-file` are inert for it (measured). That makes
# .buckconfig.local uniquely powerful and uniquely dangerous — a committed copy
# carrying warm-cache-rw content would make EVERY build in the repo
# remote-cache-enabled with allow_cache_uploads=true, bypassing the
# build-cache-policy resolver and the /specs/cache-warm-license.json kill-switch
# entirely, and would silently poison the integrity canary (whose cold build
# depends on running with NO overlay at all).
# NOTE the deliberate asymmetry: `.buckconfig.d/` is NOT ignored. Committed
# fragments there are the fail-closed way to ship real config, because a missing
# `--config-file` path silently succeeds (`BUILD SUCCEEDED`, exit 0) whereas a
# committed fragment is always read. Ignore the machine-local file; keep the
# committed-fragment door open.
/.buckconfig.local
# Multi-model harness journals (local process kit only).
# Retention: keep recent mm-runs for active drive/babysit debugging; prune older
# run trees locally as needed. Never commit mm-runs (gitignored); no bulk purge
# in product PRs — process-kit hygiene only.
.grok/mm-runs/
.grok/memory/
# Swarm check-daemon outputs (orchestrator main-checkout only; workers read these).
/err.txt
/.check/
# retired OMC residue (ADR-0711 Amendment B delete_permanently)
.omc/
# Swarm Delivery Law linked worktrees (ADR-0711); topology uses .worktrees/ not .claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/
# Stray agent worktrees accidentally created at the repo root (e.g. wt-1616); lanes belong under .worktrees/
/wt-*/
# Anti-friction wave (2026-08-14): local-only agent runtime state and transient dirs.
/.beads/
/.cursor/
/infra/capi/_out/
